{"body":"## Problem\n\nThe 2026-07-02 live-incident campaign (#1179, 15 merged PRs) closed the incident's root causes. Across six external review rounds, the campaign ledger, and the first post-campaign supervised live session (2026-07-06), a set of real-but-non-blocking findings accumulated. This issue is their single home (MECE — every item tracked exactly once; supersedes the scattered Section C ledger bullets). None of these block trading sessions or the position-market-lifecycle fix (tracked separately).\n\n## P1 — Required first (standing owner directive 2026-07-04)\n\n1. **Venue-policy layering sweep**: 17 Polymarket reject-text needles in `classify_entry_reject_reason` + `polymarket_*`-named fields in generic strategy evidence records move behind the provider layer. Directive: \"no policies hardcoded to venues/markets/strategies.\" Unblocked since Lane 4 landed.\n\n## P2 — Money-loop hardening\n\n2. Cross-source governor dedupe fence: route `closes_position: true` observations through the closed-position baseline regardless of the cumulative flag, with a reproduction-shaped test (raised 4× in #1238 reviews; disproven live — this venue emits no NT close for settlements — but the coupling is latent).\n3. Settlement-sink tightening: make the sink backends non-optional and delete the dead `Ok(())` skip paths (provably present under the owning predicate since #1238 F-1). Sub-item: align the `find(enforce)`-only \"enforced pool\" call sites onto a shared selector only if the selector family is hoisted.\n4. `settlement_recovery_config_from_loaded` fails soft (`Ok(None)`) when the sink exists but the bound is missing — unreachable behind the validator; make it error anyway (belt-and-suspenders).\n5. Boot-side divergence cross-check: under total store-write failure, kill-switch Armed can be laundered by restart — design an independent divergence marker channel (from #1185 round 3).\n6. Replay-acceptance cash pin: pin the durable cash surface (loss-governor accumulator / venue-truth balance) in replay acceptance, not just booking records (from #1181 round 2).\n\n## P3 — Evidence completeness & observability\n\n7. Live input-health emitter: wire event-driven input-health transitions into the live operator surface when the reference feed exposes a status-change hook (v1 renders Unobserved by design; pre-arm side live-proven 2026-07-06 and #1155 closed superseded on it).\n8. Backstop-adoption residuals: verify `PositionTruthRematerialized` linkage completeness at HEAD; make the rematerialization override take/clear instrument-scoped with a differential (Gemini finding on #1229, owner-confirmed, evidence-linkage only); direct unit test on the residual-position path (GLM nit).\n9. Spot fallback values are undated in evidence shapes (`observed_ts` discarded) — LOW.\n10. Poison-timestamp amended scope: exclude rejected observations' timestamps from `latest_event_ts` and routed publish inputs; ingest-time interval membership alone is insufficient.\n11. Resolution-feed outage race (unreproduced — reproduce first): a retry tick landing in the boundary window may record a false outage that suppresses a real settlement. NOTE: partially reshaped by the position-market-lifecycle fix (separate issue) — re-evaluate the residual after it lands.\n12. **Replay tooling for captured market data** (from the 2026-07-06 live session): the node captures full order-book delta / quote / index streams as feather files; build a reader that reconstructs book state at any timestamp so incidents can be replayed from our own capture instead of argued from memory.\n13. **Decision-evidence volume governance** (from the 2026-07-06 live session): `order-intents.jsonl` grows ~5KB/line at full tick rate (~2 GB observed; tens of MB/min under load) with no rotation. Fine for supervised sessions; needs rotation/compaction + the recovery readers taught to span rotated segments before long unattended runs.\n\n## P4 — Reconciler / venue-truth robustness\n\n14. Reconciliation-fill ambiguity: verify the adapter never emits `fill.reconciliation` on this venue, else add the defensive guard (from #1185 round 3).\n15. Allowance explanation-budget: unbounded drainable allowance pool on a never-decrementing-allowance venue — alarm-sensitivity, not money-safety; revisit with venue-mode evidence or a structural drain.\n16. Archetype-entrypoint E2E: prove the capital-pool → strategy settlement currency/account mapping through `register_runtime_strategy`, not a test helper (GLM, #1238 round 4).\n\n## P5 — Platform / governance\n\n17. Runtime-literal registry redesign (owner-raised 2026-07-05): 20k-line registry → sanctioned vocabulary modules auto-exempted by the verifier; registry shrinks to true exceptions. Design sketch in the #1179 ledger; likely splits into its own issue when picked up.\n18. Doctests never run in CI: the `compile_fail` timestamp-domain guarantees are enforced by nothing — add doctest execution (coordinate with the CI series; preflight guard-profile extension is deliberately NOT here — it lands as scope on #1252).\n19. Lane 3 forward traps (governed enum variant for live_submit_governance, ungoverned registration helpers, first-pool-only capital admission, venue cardinality) — design notes that spring when multi-venue/governed profiles become real.\n20. Multi-venue `VenueEventMs` clock-skew starvation — design note.\n21. #1189 verification note (LOW): confirm startup validation rejects the all-sources-unavailable reference config shape.\n\n## Verification\n\nEach item carries its acceptance shape inline; items landing as PRs go through the standard owner + external review pipeline. Re-evaluate items 2/11 after the position-market-lifecycle fix merges.\n\n## Relations\n\nRelated to #1179. Related to #1252 (item 18 boundary). Context: #1238 review rounds, #1229 review rounds, 2026-07-06 supervised session records.\n","labels":[],"number":1275,"state":"OPEN","title":"#1179 follow-ups: consolidated post-campaign hardening (settl