{"body":"## Problem\n\nThe 2026-07-02 supervised live test (Polymarket 5-minute binary, `binary_oracle_edge_taker`, $50 account) surfaced ~20 verified defects from one 6-minute run. The trading signal itself was correct (the targeted market resolved in the strategy's favor), but the substrate failed around it:\n\n- 447 entry submits in 53s for ONE opportunity; 435 venue-rejected: HTTP 400 `invalid amounts, the market buy orders maker amount supports a max accuracy of 2 decimals` (venue applies market-BUY rules to FOK BUY; our config forces limit+FOK+base-share shape); 6 below the venue $1 minimum; 40 exit SELLs rejected `not enough balance` (sells for unheld shares).\n- 37/43 exits were `exit_fail_closed` liquidations of winning positions at −11..−14% vs own fair value, triggered by a ~107ms cross-clock artifact (`rejected_future_dated` RV gate); 6 more from asymmetric hold-vs-exit valuation.\n- Admission passed $1,045 cumulative notional against a $50 account with all exposure controls unengaged.\n- Strategy inputs (reference price) missing in 91–96% of snapshots on BOTH live days (06-20 and 07-02).\n- 06-20 shows the same storm class (15,349 intents; loss governor absorbed 14,575) — chronic, not new.\n\nAdversarially-reviewed root causes (three independent review passes; load-bearing claims re-verified at tag v0.1.5):\n\n1. **Open loops at every boundary** — the system issues commands and structurally ignores what comes back: rejects leave zero cross-order state (`on_order_rejected` discards `event.reason`; cooldown arms only via `record_market_fill`); venue truth (REST positions/balance/open-orders in `venue_account_state_source.rs`, `collateral_accounting_source.rs`) is fetched once pre-run then discarded; settlement/redemption is never booked (no settle path in the taker; `on_position_closed` only flips Flat); pending order states carry no deadlines (`exposure.rs` `PendingEntryState`/`PendingExitState`), so one dropped terminal event wedges the state machine permanently.\n2. **Belief has no owner anchored to reality** — money/position/time beliefs live in caches re-seeded from the lossy NT event stream; the runtime governor binds to NT `AccountState` push that the Polymarket adapter never emits; three clock domains (venue event / local receive / NT strategy clock) compared ad hoc.\n3. **Exit-valuation modeling bias** (standalone): hold-EV gets a full uncertainty-band haircut (`current_hold_ev_bps_at` → `compute_worst_case_ev_bps`) while exit-EV uses raw book price; hysteresis favors exit (`evaluate_exit_decision`: `exit_ev >= hold_ev - exit_hysteresis_bps`); ANY missing input in the 9-step hold-EV chain defaults to liquidation.\n4. **Data plane silently null** (standalone): input publication path drops/never-populates snapshot fields; must be fixed FIRST (nothing downstream is testable at ~3% visibility). Open classification question: evaluated-and-missing vs not-evaluated recording semantics.\n\n## Expected Outcome\n\nOne campaign, six lanes, one acceptance bar. Done = the acceptance bar passes; no per-symptom issues.\n\n**Lanes** (each PR marks `Part of` this issue; never closing keywords):\n- **Lane 0 — feeds/input visibility (FIRST):** classify then fix the empty-snapshot path; single timestamp-domain module (which clock each stamp belongs to; same-domain comparisons only); fix RV ingest rejections (`reject_observation` cross-clock drops); \"sighted fraction\" means admitted-state sightedness (`fair_probability` present / `pricing_blocked_by` empty), not raw field presence; observed-value fields describe what the strategy SAW, while `pricing_blocked_by` + `fast_venue_available` describe what it could USE; residual slice 2: verify and, if needed, fix spot/reference strategy-input recording because RV unblocking alone does not mechanically populate those fields; residual slice 3: fix reference-current-price liveness: a frozen/dead stream must recover (resubscribe/refresh not suppressed by the presence of one stale quote), with the classification comment as the anchor (https://github.com/seungpyoson/bolt-v2/issues/1179#issuecomment-4868551689). Lane 0 is not complete until slice 3 lands.\n- **Lane 1 — venue-conformant entries:** dollar-sized market/quote-quantity BUYs (2-decimal maker, $1 min; NT market path already conforms); delete the two PR #480 `is_quote_quantity` fences; rejects become information — malformed → fatal loud stop; unfillable → re-decide only on changed book; structural rule: never retry an unchanged hard-rejected action.\n- **Lane 2 — exit valuation:** symmetric hold-vs-exit valuation; fix hysteresis direction; missing input → hold + loud report (never liquidate-by-default); apply Lane 0 clock policy to `classify_rv_gate` (consumption side — ingest alone is insufficient); consumption-side same-domain freshness check required (reuse existing `max_source_age_ms` semantics at the gate) because #1180 removes the ingest lag gate.\n- **Lane 3 — money loop closed:** runtime venue REST poller = continuous truth (authority inversion; NT events advisory); divergence = venue observation unexplainable by our recorded in-flight actions → whole-node halt + alarm (no tolerance bands); explicit governance-mode declaration (undeclared-ungoverned with submit-capable strategies = refuse boot); exit qty clamped at the boundary to freshly observed holdings; settlement booked at resolution.\n- **Lane 4 — order-lifecycle reconciler:** deadlines on pending states; quantity-based (not boolean) partial-fill tracking; restart re-adopts open ORDERS (bootstrap currently reads positions only).\n- **Lane 5 — evidence & health:** shutdown drain for the evidence writer (no flush path today); single confusion-state owner rendered as an operator-legible health surface (healthy/degraded/halted + why).\n\n## Acceptance Bar (all required)\n\n1. Four deterministic replay tests in CI (landed red-then-green): dropped terminal event; partial-fill-then-expire exit; restart with open order+position; hold-to-resolution settlement.\n2. One deliberately ADVERSE supervised live run (e.g., kill+restart mid-position, or hold to resolution) — not a happy-path run.\n3. Mechanical post-run assertion: bot's recorded realized cash == venue/on-chain cash delta.\n4. Any missing strategy input (strike, reference, spot, RV) produces a loud, machine-readable, operator-visible state, distinguishable from warmup, before arming (supersedes PR #1155; that PR closes when this is verified).\n5. A dead or credential-rejected feed announces itself with its reason (including IP-allowlist classification), never silently absent (extracted from PR #1156, closed).\n\n## Approach Notes\n\n- No gates/caps/thresholds as fixes. Litmus: a human-chosen number that a loss teaches you was wrong = gate (rejected); a parameter-free invariant that fails loud at violation = structural (required). Zero tolerance is the structural signature; any tolerance band is a gate.\n- Loss governor stays OFF for supervised deposit-capped tests (deposit is the loss bound) — as an explicit declared mode per Lane 3.\n- Non-goals: threshold tuning (edge threshold set from graded run data only, after feeds are fixed); new probe binaries (see #1155/#1156 dispositions); monolith decomposition (mod.rs is 5,865 lines; not the bottleneck).\n\n## Risks\n\n- Lane 3 authority inversion touches live order flow — highest blast radius; staged PRs (poller → governance declaration → clamp → settlement), each independently revertable.\n- Lanes 1/2/4 share `src/strategies/binary_oracle_edge_taker/` — implement sequentially in one session to avoid conflicts (Wave 2).\n- Removing the #480 fences resurfaces their original concerns (egress fanout, stale-cache sizing) — both must be solved inside the new behavior, not re-fenced.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun evidence (read-only) on instance i-0d544aeb04c3824e4 (eu-west-2): `/srv/bolt-v2/var/bolt-v3-live/catalog/bolt-v3/decision-evidence/order-intents.jsonl` (1.5 GB; kinds: strategy_input_snapshot / order_intent / admission_decision / exit_evaluation / exit_decision / entry_skip) and `/srv/bolt-v2/var/bolt-v3-live/catalog/live/5f05f657-*/{order_events,accounts,position_events}/`. Venue reject strings captured verbatim in `order_events/events.jsonl` (`payload_json.Rejected.reason`). All code anchors valid at tag v0.1.5 — re-verify at HEAD before use.\n\n## Relations\n\nRelated to #758\nRelated to #235\nRelated to #630\nContext: PR #480 (origin of the entry-shape fences), PR #1155 (parked; superseded by acceptance item 4), PR #1156 (closed; extracted into acceptance item 5).\n\n\n","labels":[],"number":1179,"state":"OPEN","title":"Live-trade incident 2026-07-02: consolidated fix campaign (6 lanes, single acceptance bar)","url":"https://github.com/seungpyoson/bolt-v2/issues/1179"}

