{"body":"## Problem\n\nLive measurement on 2026-07-10 found the decision-evidence file growing 760 MB in 24 minutes—approximately 100 multi-kilobyte records per second in a mostly idle session.\n\nRestart recovery reads only the final configured 1 MiB and fails closed. Per-tick noise can therefore evict recovery-critical evidence from the readable tail regardless of available disk capacity. This blocks the 24-hour soak's kill/restart acceptance leg.\n\nThe scope is the complete class: every disk-append path reachable from quote, book, timer, or index-price handlers in strategy and live-node modules—not only the currently dominant record kind.\n\n## Expected Outcome\n\n- Enumerate every decision-evidence append path, covering the complete record-kind set, plus every non-evidence per-tick appender.\n- Classify each append path exactly once as:\n  1. EVENT-KEYED\n  2. STATE-OBSERVATION\n  3. ALREADY-DEDUPED\n  4. NO NAMED READER\n- Include handler reachability, named readers, repeat semantics, dedupe-key evidence, and structurally distinct call sites in the PR table.\n- Preserve all action-, recovery-, reconciliation-, lifecycle-, reservation-, settlement-, and booking-error evidence.\n- State-change-key the blocked-RV `strategy_input_snapshot` path.\n- Leave submit-linked `strategy_input_snapshot` records untouched.\n- Verify existing per-tick dedupe keys contain no timestamps, prices, ages, counters, or other tick-varying fields.\n- Flag paths without named readers for an owner decision; do not silently remove them.\n\n## Approach Notes\n\n`strategy_input_snapshot` has two structural append paths:\n\n- Submit-linked snapshots come from `entry_strategy_input_evidence_snapshot_at`, carry a non-empty `client_order_id`, and are consumed by recovery and shadow-PnL. They remain EVENT-KEYED and untouched.\n- Blocked-RV snapshots come from `blocked_entry_strategy_input_evidence_snapshot_at`, carry an empty `client_order_id`, and have no machine consumer. They retain forensic value through full RV diagnostics, so they remain present but become STATE-OBSERVATION records keyed on semantic state.\n\nAdd a strategy-local blocked-snapshot key containing market/selection identity, blocker categories, availability state, RV surface/blockers, and normalized per-source status. Exclude prices, timestamps, ages, sample/rejection counts, coverage, and volatility values.\n\nClear the key when the strategy leaves the blocked-RV condition. In-memory keys reset on restart; one duplicate per key per process lifetime is accepted, matching the #1351 terminal-evidence ruling.\n\nThe PR must document the reproducible source sweep used to establish that no non-evidence disk appenders exist in the strategy/live-node handlers and explicitly cover quote, book, timer, and index-price reachability.\n\n## Non-Goals\n\n- Capture module changes\n- Rotation or compaction\n- Journald changes\n- Uploader changes\n- Recovery byte-limit changes\n- Evidence schema changes\n- Writer-level dedupe\n\n## Risks\n\nThe primary risk is accidentally suppressing submit-linked recovery evidence. The design prevents this structurally by applying dedupe only at the distinct blocked-snapshot call site.\n\nA second risk is vacuous dedupe. Tests and the PR census must prove all relevant keys exclude per-tick-varying observations.\n\n## Verification\n\n- RED differential on current code: N identical blocked evaluations emit more than one snapshot.\n- GREEN differential: N identical blocked evaluations emit exactly one snapshot; a semantic state change emits the second.\n- Submit-linked snapshots remain complete.\n- Audit bucket-3 keys and differentials for entry-skip, exit-decision, exit-outcome, and requote-throttle.\n- Full unfiltered suite at exact head, with no scope filters.\n- `just fmt-check`.\n- Runtime-literal self-test and audit if strings change.\n- Static/source-fence checks.\n- PR reports exact head SHA and the exhaustive bucket table.\n\n## Relations\n\nRelated to #1275\nRelated to #1179\n","labels":[],"number":1354,"state":"OPEN","title":"Eliminate per-tick disk writes by append-path class","url":"https://github.com/seungpyoson/bolt-v2/issues/1354"}
